    "transcript": "Why is the food steaming, but the plate's still cool? Microwaves tug the water molecules inside food back and forth, and that makes heat. Glass and microwave-safe ceramics barely absorb them. The hot food warms the plate, but water soaked into porous clay or an iron-rich glaze can make pottery heat itself. To test a dish, heat it empty beside a cup of water for one minute. If it stays cool, it's safe. Download Recall for learning any new subject with AI.",
